00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:04.390 align:start position:0%
voters in the u.s have been casting  ballots for either joe biden or donald  trump  but to be president they'll need to win  the electoral college  not necessarily the most votes across  the u.s  so how does the electoral college work  that college is made up of 538 electors  they're people chosen from each state  the number of electors each state gets  depends on how many members of congress  it has  so california has 55 but vermont only  has three  now whether a state's electors are  republican or democrat  depends on which candidate gets the most  votes in that state  so let's take california as an example  say a majority of californians vote for  joe biden  he wins the popular vote there in that  case all of california's 55 electors  are going to be democrats it's winner  takes all no matter how small the  majority  those 55 democrat electors are then  obliged to vote for biden  to become president trump or biden has  to get at least 270 electoral votes  that's just over half  so it's the electoral college that  matters not winning the popular vote  and 2016 is a good example of that  back then some said clinton's chances of  winning were high  but she didn't win that's because while  clinton got more votes overall  what's called the popular vote she lost  the electoral college  in almost every presidential election  the  winner of the national popular vote  has also won the electoral college what  happened in 2016  was extremely rare donald trump beat  hillary clinton in michigan pennsylvania  and wisconsin by a total of just under  80 000 votes  but he ended up getting all 46 electoral  votes in those three states  it helped him cross the 270 mark to win  even though hillary clinton got more  votes overall  nearly 3 million more here's the other  thing to watch out for  some states are expected to be easy wins  for trump or biden  but the tight races will be in what are  called battleground states or the vote  could go either way  and together they make up a lot of  electoral votes that could tip the  outcome  keep an eye out for more videos from the  start here team on al jazeera's facebook  and instagram stories  and our twitter feed where we'll bring  you updates throughout election night  [Music]
 

